===========================================================================
AI models
===========================================================================

AI models are not part of this repository. Each model is subject to its own
licence, which Silberkorn shows together with its source before
downloading.

Real-ESRGAN (models realesr-general-x4v3, realesr-general-wdn-x4v3,
RealESRGAN_x4plus)
  Copyright (c) 2021, Xintao Wang
  Licence: BSD 3-Clause
  https://github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN
  The official weights are converted to ONNX with
  werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py; the network architectures are
  re-implemented there. The converted model files are published as assets
  of the release "modelle-1" of this project, together with the BSD 3-Clause
  licence text of Real-ESRGAN (LICENSE-Real-ESRGAN.txt), which Silberkorn
  also downloads and stores next to the models.

SCUNet (model scunet_color_real_psnr)
  Copyright 2022 Kai Zhang
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/cszn/SCUNet
  The official weights (published in the release v1.0 of
  https://github.com/cszn/KAIR) are converted to ONNX with
  werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py. The network architecture is
  re-implemented there without einops and timm; as a change to the original,
  the attention mask of the shifted windows is computed from coordinates and
  the padding to multiples of 64 is done outside the network, so the ONNX
  model accepts any image size. The weights themselves are unchanged. The
  converted model file is published as an asset of the release "modelle-2"
  of this project, together with the Apache 2.0 licence text of SCUNet
  (LICENSE-SCUNet.txt), which Silberkorn also downloads and stores next to
  the model.

Restormer (model single_image_defocus_deblurring)
  Copyright (c) 2022 Syed Waqas Zamir and contributors
  Licence: MIT License
  https://github.com/swz30/Restormer
  The official weights (release v1.0 of the repository above) are converted
  to ONNX with werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py. The network architecture is
  re-implemented there without einops; as a change to the original, the
  normalisation in the attention is computed as the mean of squares after
  dividing by the largest magnitude, which gives the same result but does
  not overflow in half precision (FP16). The weights themselves are
  unchanged. The converted model file is published as an asset of the
  release "modelle-3" of this project, together with the MIT licence text of
  Restormer (LICENSE-Restormer.txt), which Silberkorn also downloads and
  stores next to the model.

BiRefNet (model BiRefNet_lite-general-2K)
  Copyright (c) 2024 ZhengPeng
  Licence: MIT License
  https://github.com/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
  The official weights (release v1 of the repository above) are converted
  to ONNX with werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py. The network architecture is
  re-implemented in werkzeuge/netz_birefnet.py without einops, timm, kornia
  and torchvision. Changes to the original, all computing the same result:
  the deformable convolution (torchvision.ops.deform_conv2d) is expressed
  with grid_sample; the last 1x1 convolution is swapped with the bilinear
  upscaling before it and merged with the linear input branch, to save
  graphics memory; the ImageNet normalisation is part of the network; the
  input size is fixed to 2560 x 1440 as in training. The weights themselves
  are unchanged. The converted model file is published as an asset of the
  release "modelle-4" of this project, together with the MIT licence text of
  BiRefNet (LICENSE-BiRefNet.txt), which Silberkorn also downloads and
  stores next to the model.

SAM 2 - Segment Anything in Images and Videos (model SAM 2.1 Hiera small)
  Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2
  The official checkpoint sam2.1_hiera_small.pt (published by Meta at
  https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/segment_anything_2/092824/) is converted to
  ONNX with werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py. werkzeuge/netz_sam2.py is
  derived from the SAM 2 source code (sam2/modeling) and is therefore also
  under the Apache License 2.0 (full text in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt); it
  contains only the parts needed for a single image - image encoder (Hiera
  and FPN neck), prompt encoder and mask decoder - without hydra, iopath
  and torchvision. Changes to the
  original, all computing the same result: the encoder has a fixed input of
  1024 x 1024, normalises the image itself and outputs the features as
  SAM2ImagePredictor.set_image stores them (with no_mem_embed and the
  high-resolution levels through conv_s0/conv_s1); the decoder takes the
  click points in pixels of the 1024 image, appends the padding point
  itself, accepts the previous mask through a 0/1 input instead of None and
  outputs all four masks with their predicted quality; attention is written
  out instead of scaled_dot_product_attention; the video parts (memory,
  object pointers, object score) are left out. The weights themselves are
  unchanged. The two converted model files (encoder and decoder) are
  published as assets of the release "modelle-5" of this project, together
  with the Apache License 2.0 text (LICENSE-SAM2.txt), which Silberkorn
  also downloads and stores next to the model.

LaMa - Resolution-robust Large Mask Inpainting with Fourier Convolutions
(model Big LaMa)
  Copyright 2021 Samsung Research
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/advimman/lama
  The official checkpoint big-lama (best.ckpt in big-lama.zip, the download
  named in the README of the repository above) is converted to ONNX with
  werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py; werkzeuge/checkpoint_lesen.py reads it
  without executing code from the pickle. werkzeuge/netz_lama.py is derived
  from the LaMa source code (saicinpainting/training/modules/ffc.py, itself
  based on the Fast Fourier Convolution, https://github.com/pkumivision/FFC)
  and is therefore also under the Apache License 2.0 (full text in
  LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). It contains only the generator and only the
  branches Big LaMa uses. Changes to the original, all computing the same
  result: the Fourier transform (torch.fft.rfftn/irfftn) is written as
  multiplication with DFT matrices built inside the network; the network
  takes image and mask separately and blanks the masked area itself. The
  weights themselves are unchanged. The converted model file is published
  as an asset of the release "modelle-6" of this project, together with the
  Apache License 2.0 text of LaMa (LICENSE-LaMa.txt), which Silberkorn
  also downloads and stores next to the model.

Depth Anything V2 (model Depth-Anything-V2-Small)
  Lihe Yang et al., 2024 - the Small model and the code are under the
  Apache License 2.0 (the larger models are not and are not used)
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/DepthAnything/Depth-Anything-V2
  https://huggingface.co/depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Small
  Contains DINOv2 (Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates,
  Apache License 2.0) and the DPT head from MiDaS/DPT (Intel ISL).
  The official weights depth_anything_v2_vits.pth are converted to ONNX
  with werkzeuge/modelle_exportieren.py. werkzeuge/netz_tiefe.py is derived
  from the Depth Anything V2 source code and is therefore also under the
  Apache License 2.0 (full text in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). Changes to the
  original, all computing the same result: the input size is fixed to
  700 x 1050 and the positional embedding is interpolated for it in
  advance, exactly as the original does at run time; the network takes
  sRGB in 0..1 and normalises it itself; xFormers, the mask token path and
  training-only branches are left out. The weights themselves are
  unchanged. The converted model file is published as an asset of the
  release "modelle-7" of this project, together with the Apache License 2.0
  text (LICENSE-DepthAnythingV2.txt), which Silberkorn also downloads and
  stores next to the model.

FLUX.2 [klein] 4B with the outpaint LoRA by fal (for "Extend with AI")
  FLUX.2 [klein] 4B: Copyright Black Forest Labs
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B
  https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-4B
  flux-2-klein-4B-outpaint-lora: Copyright fal
  Licence: Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/fal/flux-2-klein-4B-outpaint-lora
  The transformer of the distilled model and the VAE are converted to ONNX
  with werkzeuge/outpaint_export.py, which uses diffusers and contains no
  code of the originals. Changes to the originals: the LoRA is merged into
  the transformer weights with a scale of 1.1; the weights of its matrix
  multiplications are quantised to 8-bit integers (MatMulNBits, block size
  128), its other weights and the VAE are stored in 16-bit floating point;
  for the export, rotary embedding and RMSNorm are written out as plain
  operations computing the same result; the VAE encoder returns the mean of
  the latent distribution and both VAE parts take and return images in
  0..1. The embedding of the fixed prompt "Fill the green spaces according
  to the image", computed with the text encoder of FLUX.2 [klein] base 4B
  (Qwen3, Apache License 2.0), is stored together with the batch-norm
  statistics of the VAE and the scheduler settings. The converted files are
  published as assets of the release "modelle-8" of this project, the
  transformer weights split into several files, together with the Apache
  License 2.0 text (LICENSE-FLUX2-klein.txt) and a notice of these changes
  (NOTICE-FLUX2-klein.txt, also in LICENSES/), which Silberkorn also
  downloads and stores next to the model.

